  "readOnlyHint": false,
  "title": "Sign out"
 },
 "description": "Wipe the persistent credentials file at `~/.log10x/credentials` and reload envs so subsequent calls fall back to demo mode (or whichever lower-priority configuration source picks up). **Call this for**: \"sign me out of Log10x\", \"log out\", \"remove my Log10x credentials\", \"stop using my Log10x account\", \"go back to demo mode\". Idempotent \u2014 running it without saved credentials is a no-op. Does NOT revoke the API key on the BE; the user must do that from console.log10x.com \u2192 Profile \u2192 API Settings if they want to invalidate the key everywhere (mirrors `gh auth logout` and `aws sso logout`). If the user has `LOG10X_API_KEY` set in their MCP host config, that env var will still be active after sign-out \u2014 the tool result will flag this so the LLM can tell the user to also unset it and restart.",
 "execution": {
  "taskSupport": "forbidden"
 },
